Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage to compute bowling average (runs conceded ÷ wickets taken):

• ball_by_ball.bowler : identifies the bowler for every legal delivery.  
• batsman_scored.runs_scored : runs off the bat conceded on that ball (join on match_id/over_id/ball_id/innings_no).  
• extra_runs.extra_runs : extra runs; wides & no‑balls count against the bowler (a refined query could filter on extra_type IN ('wides','noballs')).  
• wicket_taken.player_out (+ join with ball_by_ball for the bowler) : tells on which balls a wicket fell and therefore credits that wicket to the current bowler.  
• player.player_id / player.player_name : map bowler‑id to human‑readable name.  

Typical conditions / join keys to link ball‑by‑ball with the auxiliary tables  
ON b.match_id = x.match_id  
AND b.over_id  = x.over_id  
AND b.ball_id  = x.ball_id  
AND b.innings_no = x.innings_no  

Below are ten exploratory → final SQL snippets (all capped with LIMIT 20 for safety).  

```sql
--1. Preview a handful of deliveries and the bowler involved
SELECT DISTINCT bowler
FROM ball_by_ball
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. Count how many legal balls each bowler delivered
SELECT bowler, COUNT(*) AS balls_bowled
FROM ball_by_ball
GROUP BY bowler
ORDER BY balls_bowled DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. List first 20 wicket events together with the bowler who took them
SELECT b.bowler, w.player_out, w.kind_out
FROM wicket_taken AS w
JOIN ball_by_ball AS b
  ON b.match_id = w.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
 AND b.innings_no = w.innings_no
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Number of wickets credited to each bowler
SELECT b.bowler, COUNT(*) AS wickets
FROM wicket_taken AS w
JOIN ball_by_ball AS b
  ON b.match_id = w.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
 AND b.innings_no = w.innings_no
GROUP BY b.bowler
ORDER BY wickets DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Runs‑off‑the‑bat conceded by every bowler
SELECT b.bowler, SUM(bs.runs_scored) AS runs_off_bat
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
  ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
 AND b.innings_no = bs.innings_no
GROUP BY b.bowler
ORDER BY runs_off_bat DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6. Extra runs (wides & no‑balls) that count against each bowler
SELECT b.bowler, SUM(er.extra_runs) AS extra_runs_against
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN extra_runs AS er
  ON b.match_id = er.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = er.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = er.ball_id
 AND b.innings_no = er.innings_no
WHERE er.extra_type IN ('wides','noballs')
GROUP BY b.bowler
ORDER BY extra_runs_against DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7. Combine runs‑off‑the‑bat and penalised extras for each bowler
WITH bat AS (
    SELECT b.bowler, SUM(bs.runs_scored) AS bat_runs
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
      ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
     AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
     AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = bs.innings_no
    GROUP BY b.bowler
),
ext AS (
    SELECT b.bowler, SUM(er.extra_runs) AS extra_runs
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN extra_runs AS er
      ON b.match_id = er.match_id
     AND b.over_id  = er.over_id
     AND b.ball_id  = er.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = er.innings_no
    WHERE er.extra_type IN ('wides','noballs')
    GROUP BY b.bowler
)
SELECT bat.bowler,
       COALESCE(bat.bat_runs,0) + COALESCE(ext.extra_runs,0) AS total_runs_conceded
FROM bat
LEFT JOIN ext USING(bowler)
ORDER BY total_runs_conceded DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8. Merge total runs with wicket counts to compute each bowler's average
WITH wk AS (
    SELECT b.bowler, COUNT(*) AS wickets
    FROM wicket_taken AS w
    JOIN ball_by_ball AS b
      ON b.match_id = w.match_id
     AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
     AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = w.innings_no
    GROUP BY b.bowler
),
rn AS (
    SELECT b.bowler,
           SUM(bs.runs_scored) AS bat_runs
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
      ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
     AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
     AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = bs.innings_no
    GROUP BY b.bowler
),
ex AS (
    SELECT b.bowler,
           SUM(er.extra_runs) AS extra_runs
    FROM ball_by_ball AS b
    JOIN extra_runs AS er
      ON b.match_id = er.match_id
     AND b.over_id  = er.over_id
     AND b.ball_id  = er.ball_id
     AND b.innings_no = er.innings_no
    WHERE er.extra_type IN ('wides','noballs')
    GROUP BY b.bowler
)
SELECT wk.bowler,
       (COALESCE(rn.bat_runs,0) + COALESCE(ex.extra_runs,0)) AS runs_conceded,
       wk.wickets,
       ROUND(1.0 * (COALESCE(rn.bat_runs,0) + COALESCE(ex.extra_runs,0)) / wk.wickets, 2) AS bowling_average
FROM wk
LEFT JOIN rn USING(bowler)
LEFT JOIN ex USING(bowler)
WHERE wk.wickets > 0
ORDER BY bowling_average ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
